 partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}$ at $(1,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(1,0) & =1\\cdot {e}^{1\\cdot 0}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡0 \\\\  & =1\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(1,0)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(1,0)}(y-0) \\\\ z-(-1) & =(-1)y \\\\ z & =-y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(1,0,-1)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=1 \\\\ z &=-y-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186407317 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407319 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407317 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8482a7f1-9b85-58c1-b946-6953c47668a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407317 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407318 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407318 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e1916473-66ad-5022-aafa-9787da440dac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407318 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186125183 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407319 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f2c84ac0-3b38-584c-9809-dfa6181b9351" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407319 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186338917 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425089 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186425121 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425089 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186425122 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425089 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186425123 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425089 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186425124 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425089 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186425125 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425089 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425089 #edb/ref 1045 "Geometric Interpretations of Partial Derivatives" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425089 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186425122 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425089 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 1